---
layout: base.njk
bodyClass: docs-examples-page
title: Examples
description: Complete interfaces built only from semantic HTML and Cirth, from app navigation and dashboards to checkout, articles and pricing. Every block shows its exact source.
---
{#- A showcase, not a documentation page: no sidebar and no pager, and a
    wider stage, because a dashboard or a checkout needs the room to look
    like one. The examples themselves are data (_data/examples.js) rendered
    through the same `demo` shortcode as every other live example, so each
    block's "Show HTML" is the exact markup on screen, styled by the
    stylesheet this site loads with nothing added. -#}
<main id="main-content" class="container docs-showcase-page" data-pagefind-body>
	<header class="docs-showcase-intro">
		<h1>Examples</h1>
		<p>
			Complete screens built from the elements documented on this site and
			nothing else: no example below adds a stylesheet of its own. Each one
			is rendered live by the stylesheet this page loads, follows the theme
			and preset you pick in the header, and opens its exact source under
			<strong>Show HTML</strong>.
		</p>
		<nav aria-label="Example categories" class="docs-chip-nav">
			<ul>
				{% for category in examples %}
					<li><a href="#{{ category.id }}">{{ category.title }}</a></li>
				{% endfor %}
				<li><a href="#builds">Builds</a></li>
			</ul>
		</nav>
	</header>

	{% for category in examples %}
		<section class="docs-example-category" id="{{ category.id }}" aria-labelledby="{{ category.id }}-title">
			<header>
				<h2 id="{{ category.id }}-title">{{ category.title }}</h2>
				<p>{{ category.summary }}</p>
			</header>
			{% for item in category.items %}
				<section class="docs-example-block" aria-labelledby="{{ item.demo }}-title">
					<header>
						<h3 id="{{ item.demo }}-title">{{ item.title }}</h3>
						<p>{{ item.summary }}</p>
						<p class="docs-example-uses">
							<span>Built from</span>
							{% for use in item.uses %}<a href="{{ use.link }}">{{ use.text }}</a>{% endfor %}
						</p>
					</header>
					{% demo item.demo, "default", item.frame or "" %}
				</section>
			{% endfor %}
		</section>
	{% endfor %}

	<section class="docs-example-category" id="builds" aria-labelledby="builds-title">
		<header>
			<h2 id="builds-title">One interface, four builds</h2>
			<p>
				The same sign-in form under each published build. Every frame is
				isolated from this site and loads a stylesheet compiled from
				<code>src/</code> with the switches of the real entry point.
			</p>
		</header>
		<div class="docs-build-comparison">
			<div>
				<figure><figcaption><strong>Default</strong><code>cirth.min.css</code></figcaption><iframe tabindex="-1" title="Default Cirth build example" src="/lab/default/?theme=light"></iframe></figure>
				<figure><figcaption><strong>Classless</strong><code>cirth.classless.min.css</code></figcaption><iframe tabindex="-1" title="Classless Cirth build example" src="/lab/classless/?theme=light"></iframe></figure>
				<figure><figcaption><strong>Scoped</strong><code>cirth.scoped.min.css</code></figcaption><iframe tabindex="-1" title="Scoped Cirth build example" src="/lab/scoped/?theme=dark"></iframe></figure>
				<figure><figcaption><strong>Scoped + classless</strong><code>cirth.classless.scoped.min.css</code></figcaption><iframe tabindex="-1" title="Scoped classless Cirth build example" src="/lab/scoped-classless/?theme=dark"></iframe></figure>
			</div>
			<footer>No documentation JavaScript is needed for these frames: theme and build are separate static URLs.</footer>
		</div>
	</section>

	<footer class="docs-showcase-next">
		<p>Every element in these screens has its own page with the details.</p>
		<p class="docs-hero-actions">
			<a href="/installation" role="button">Install Cirth</a>
			<a href="/components/accordion" role="button" class="secondary outline">Browse components</a>
		</p>
	</footer>
</main>
